1.67.m:
His fields are the bodies, and the seed is good and evil deeds;
He knows them, being the self of yoga, hence he is called the knower of the field (kṣetrajña).
He lies in the unmanifest citadel, and therefore he is remembered as the spirit (puruṣa).

For he is said to be all-pervading and also without qualities;
Knowing him thus, I worship that eternal Self,
Bhāskara, lord of the gods of gods, lord of all beings, Acyuta.

1.68.m:
One goes to the world of the Sun in a vehicle yoked with swans;
With thousands of śatapuṣpa flowers, one goes to the world of Pūṣan;
With baka flowers, O best of the twice-born, one goes to the world of Bhānu.
